  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marismas Nacionales 2-Migbirdgrants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Nayarit Marismas Nacionales Biosphere Reserve was decreed in May, 2010, and includes 330,760 acres under the protection of the Mexican Federal Protected Area System. There is and there will continue to be public access to the sites included in the project. The registered avifauna at Marismas Nacionales is a total 446 species, 43% of the total number of species reported for all of Mexico. Marismas Nacionales is habitat for 4.5% of the aquatic migratory birds wintering in Mexico and hosts 19.6% of the shorebirds migrating or wintering along the Pacific coast of Mexico. The project will: 1) protect habitat on 19,768 acres using ecological easements; 2) restore water flow in canals to impact 741 acres; 3) conduct formal and non-formal environmental training and awareness for 200 teachers and 20,000 individuals participating in educational events; 4) develop a legal framework for a freshwater conservation strategy; and 5) continue bird monitoring.</narrative>
  </description>
